WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.950
The Jackson family are on holiday in Turkey.

00:04.000 --> 00:07.950
They're staying at a big hotel in Istanbul.

00:08.000 --> 00:15.950
Mark, 13, his sister Fay, 12, and their parents like Turkey.

00:16.000 --> 00:20.950
It's beautiful, the weather's hot, and the food's good.

00:21.000 --> 00:23.950
There's a lot to see, too.

00:24.000 --> 00:28.000
Today, they're visiting the city of Troy.

00:29.000 --> 00:30.950
It's 9 o'clock in the morning.

00:31.000 --> 00:36.000
They're getting on a bus in front of their hotel.

00:38.000 --> 00:40.950
There are 40 people on the bus.

00:41.000 --> 00:47.000
They come from Britain, America, France, Italy, and Holland.

00:53.000 --> 00:55.950
At Troy, they all have lunch.

00:56.000 --> 00:58.950
Then they start to look at the old city.

00:59.000 --> 01:01.950
It's a very hot day.

01:02.000 --> 01:06.950
After an hour, Mark sits under a tree.

01:07.000 --> 01:11.950
I'm going to stop here for a moment. He tells Fay.

01:12.000 --> 01:15.950
Okay, she answers.

01:16.000 --> 01:18.950
Then Mark sees something on the ground.

01:19.000 --> 01:22.950
What's that? He thinks.

01:23.000 --> 01:25.950
It's a flat, yellow stone.

01:26.000 --> 01:27.950
Mark picks it up.

01:28.000 --> 01:31.950
Then he starts to clean it with his hands.

01:32.000 --> 01:36.950
But I know this stone, he thinks.

01:37.000 --> 01:39.950
It comes from... from...

01:40.000 --> 01:43.950
Suddenly, there's a white light in his eyes.

01:44.000 --> 01:45.950
Mark closes them.

01:46.000 --> 01:47.950
The light's strong.

01:48.000 --> 01:51.950
Now there's a loud wind in his ears.

01:52.000 --> 01:55.950
He can't hear or see anything.

01:56.000 --> 01:59.950
What's happening? He thinks.

02:00.000 --> 02:04.950
Ten seconds later, the light and the wind stop.

02:05.000 --> 02:07.950
Mark opens his eyes.

02:08.000 --> 02:09.950
He's standing on a beach.

02:10.000 --> 02:13.950
He can see hundreds of ships and men.

02:14.000 --> 02:18.950
Behind him, there's a beautiful city with high walls.

02:19.000 --> 02:22.950
Where am I? He thinks.

02:23.000 --> 02:24.950
Where's my family?

02:25.000 --> 02:28.950
He puts the yellow stone in his pocket.

02:29.000 --> 02:31.950
Then one of the men says to him,

02:32.000 --> 02:34.950
Boy, come here.

02:35.000 --> 02:36.950
Me?

02:37.000 --> 02:41.950
Mark walks across the beach to a long black ship.

02:42.000 --> 02:45.950
Carry this. The man says.

02:46.000 --> 02:48.950
He gives Mark a lot of wood.

02:49.000 --> 02:50.950
Then he gets off the ship.

02:51.000 --> 02:53.950
Follow me, he says.

02:54.000 --> 02:56.950
Mark follows him.

02:57.000 --> 03:01.950
The man's very tall and has a short brown beard.

03:02.000 --> 03:04.950
I don't know your face, he says.

03:05.000 --> 03:07.950
Are you new here?

03:08.000 --> 03:10.950
Yes, Mark answers.

03:11.000 --> 03:14.950
That's right, I'm new here.

03:15.000 --> 03:19.950
My name's Andros, says the man.

03:20.000 --> 03:23.950
He and Mark walk for another ten minutes.

03:24.000 --> 03:26.950
Then they climb a small hill.

03:27.000 --> 03:29.950
At the top, Mark stops.

03:30.000 --> 03:34.950
There, in front of them, is a big wooden horse.

03:35.000 --> 03:38.950
Andros sees Mark's face and smiles.

03:39.000 --> 03:44.950
Well, what do you think of it? He asks.

03:45.000 --> 03:46.950
Mark doesn't answer.

03:47.000 --> 03:48.950
And Andros says,

03:49.000 --> 03:54.950
This horse is going to win the war for us Greeks.

03:55.000 --> 03:56.950
They walk down the hill.

03:57.000 --> 04:00.950
There are a lot of men working under the horse.

04:01.000 --> 04:03.950
One of them talks to Andros.

04:04.000 --> 04:06.950
There's a problem, he says.

04:07.000 --> 04:10.950
We can't find a stone for the second eye.

04:11.000 --> 04:14.950
We must find one before tomorrow.

04:15.000 --> 04:18.950
Mark looks at the horse's one bright eye.

04:19.000 --> 04:22.950
Then he remembers the stone in his pocket.

04:23.000 --> 04:24.950
Wait, he says.

04:25.000 --> 04:27.950
I think I can help you.

04:28.000 --> 04:31.950
He takes the stone out of his pocket.

04:32.000 --> 04:34.950
But how? Says Andros.

04:35.000 --> 04:37.950
The man smiles.

04:38.000 --> 04:40.950
That's it. That's it.

04:41.000 --> 04:43.950
He looks at Mark.

04:44.000 --> 04:46.950
What's your name, boy?

04:47.000 --> 04:48.950
Mark tells him.

04:49.000 --> 04:51.950
He's new here, says Andros.

04:52.000 --> 04:53.950
Ah!

04:54.000 --> 04:56.950
The man's very happy.

04:57.000 --> 05:00.950
Well, we must thank him.

05:01.000 --> 05:06.950
I know you can come with us in the horse tomorrow night.

05:07.000 --> 05:09.950
Mark's mouth opens.

05:10.000 --> 05:12.950
Me?

05:13.000 --> 05:17.950
That evening, Mark sits near a big fire on the beach.

05:18.000 --> 05:20.950
There's an old woman beside him.

05:21.000 --> 05:24.950
Her name is Anna, and she's a cook.

05:25.000 --> 05:27.950
She tells Mark lots of stories.

05:28.000 --> 05:36.000
Stories about Greece, the war, and the beautiful princess, Helen.

05:37.000 --> 05:39.950
In the end, she goes to bed.

05:40.000 --> 05:43.950
Goodbye, boy. She says.

05:44.000 --> 05:46.950
Come and see me again one day.

05:47.000 --> 05:50.950
Come and see me again.

05:51.000 --> 05:54.950
Next morning, the horse is ready.

05:55.000 --> 05:57.950
Greek soldiers pull it to the gates of Troy.

05:58.000 --> 06:00.950
Then they leave it there.

06:01.000 --> 06:04.950
Inside the horse, there are 40 Greeks.

06:05.000 --> 06:09.950
They wait all afternoon under the hot yellow sun.

06:10.000 --> 06:12.950
Mark's sitting in the horse's head.

06:13.000 --> 06:16.950
What happens now? He thinks.

06:17.000 --> 06:21.000
Suddenly, the gates open.

06:27.000 --> 06:29.950
Trojan soldiers walk out.

06:30.000 --> 06:34.000
They pull the horse inside and shut the gates again.

06:36.000 --> 06:38.950
Mark can hear the Trojans.

06:39.000 --> 06:44.950
Why are the Greeks giving us this horse? Asks one.

06:45.000 --> 06:47.950
Do you think they want to end the war?

06:48.000 --> 06:53.950
Yes. Look. Says a soldier on top of the city walls.

06:54.000 --> 06:56.950
Their ships are leaving.

06:57.000 --> 07:04.000
After that, the Trojans eat, sing, and dance all evening.

07:06.000 --> 07:10.950
Then they go to bed very late, and Troy is quiet.

07:11.000 --> 07:17.950
At that moment, the Greeks climb out of the horse.

07:18.000 --> 07:21.950
Four men go to the gates and open them.

07:22.000 --> 07:26.950
A minute later, there are thousands of Greek soldiers in the city.

07:27.000 --> 07:30.950
They and their ships are back.

07:31.000 --> 07:34.950
They run from one building to another.

07:35.000 --> 07:38.950
In five minutes, Troy is on fire.

07:39.000 --> 07:41.950
Mark watches all this.

07:42.000 --> 07:45.950
Suddenly, he sees a beautiful woman.

07:46.000 --> 07:48.950
She's running along the city walls.

07:49.000 --> 07:51.950
It's Helen, he thinks.

07:52.000 --> 07:55.950
Helen of Troy.

07:56.000 --> 07:58.950
At that moment, Andros says,

07:59.000 --> 08:00.950
Follow me, boy.

08:01.000 --> 08:04.950
He runs down a small street very fast.

08:05.000 --> 08:09.950
Mark follows, but the streets full of smoke.

08:10.000 --> 08:13.950
After a minute, he can't see anything.

08:14.000 --> 08:16.950
Andros, he says,

08:17.000 --> 08:18.950
Where are you?

08:19.000 --> 08:24.950
Then suddenly, two Trojans with swords come out of the smoke.

08:25.000 --> 08:26.950
Mark looks at them.

08:27.000 --> 08:28.950
Please don't kill me.

08:29.000 --> 08:31.950
He says, don't kill me.

08:32.000 --> 08:34.950
Please.

08:35.000 --> 08:39.950
Mark, Mark, it's four o'clock.

08:40.000 --> 08:42.950
The bus is leaving in a minute.

08:43.000 --> 08:46.950
Fay is looking down at Mark.

08:47.000 --> 08:50.950
After a moment, he suddenly wakes up.

08:51.000 --> 08:54.950
What? He asks.

08:55.000 --> 08:58.950
The bus is leaving. Fay says again.

08:59.000 --> 09:00.950
Then she asks,

09:01.000 --> 09:02.950
Are you okay?

09:03.000 --> 09:04.950
Your face is white.

09:05.000 --> 09:07.950
And what's that dirty stone?

09:08.000 --> 09:11.950
Mark looks at the yellow stone in his hand.

09:12.000 --> 09:12.950
This?

09:13.000 --> 09:17.950
Oh, it's nothing. He says.

09:18.000 --> 09:19.950
Mark stands up.

09:20.000 --> 09:22.950
He sees an old woman.

09:23.000 --> 09:27.950
She has lots of small wooden horses in a basket.

09:28.000 --> 09:31.950
Do you want one boy? She asks.

09:32.000 --> 09:34.950
Yes, why not?

09:35.000 --> 09:38.950
Mark buys a horse and looks at the woman.

09:39.000 --> 09:43.950
No, it can't be. He thinks.

09:44.000 --> 09:46.950
He walks to the bus.

09:47.000 --> 09:50.950
Behind him, the old woman smiles.

09:51.000 --> 09:54.950
Goodbye, boy. She says.

09:55.000 --> 09:57.950
Come and see me again one day.

09:58.000 --> 10:01.000
Come and see me again.
